  "markdown_content": "## Air Quality Crisis\\nFamilies in New Delhi are grappling with severe air pollution that has turned the Indian capital into one of the world's most polluted cities. The crisis is particularly affecting children, leading parents to make tough choices about their future.\\n\\n## Impact on Families\\n> \"The decision comes as pollution levels continue to pose serious health risks, especially to young developing lungs,\" says Amrita Rosha, a 45-year-old mother who has decided to leave the city with her two children - 4-year-old Vanaaya and 9-year-old Abhiraj.\\n\\n## Environmental Exodus\\nThe city's air quality has deteriorated significantly, with pollution levels frequently reaching hazardous levels that far exceed World Health Organization guidelines. This environmental crisis has created a new category of pollution refugees - families forced to relocate simply to protect their children's health.",
